# Hatch Tooltips
gt.blockmachines.hatch.nuclearbus.desc=Nuclear core bus for items\nHolds fuel rods, reflectors, coolant cells, control rods, or insulators\nInput-only core component bus\nOutputs eject to reactor output buses and hatches
gt.blockmachines.hatch.nuclearhatch.desc=Tiered nuclear fluid hatch (%s)\nHolds input coolant or liquid nuclear fuel\nInput-only core fluid hatch\nAll outputs (steam, hot coolant, byproducts, spent fuel) eject to reactor output hatches\nCapacity: %s L\nCoolant boiling and transmutation under neutron flux\nConductance: %s EU/(t·°C)\nItem pipe casing determines allowed coolants\nInserting coolant into a dry superheated reactor will cause thermal shock!
gt.blockmachines.hatch.nuclearhighpressure.desc=Hermetic core passage endpoint for closed coolant loops\nConnects top inlet to bottom outlet for external heat exchange loops\nPairs strictly by column coordinates (Slice 0 top <-> Slice 4 bottom)\nAccepts coolant flow from pumps and heat exchangers without storing fluids
gt.blockmachines.hatch.nuclearcontrol.desc=Emits redstone signals based on nuclear reactor conditions\nRight-click with screwdriver to cycle metric (sneak+right-click for bundled mode)\nRight-click with soldering iron to cycle statistic\nOutputs 0-15 vanilla redstone or 0-255 ProjectRed bundled signals strictly from front face\nSupports 16-channel ProjectRed bundled cables with 8-bit precision
gt.blockmachines.hatch.nuclearcontrolrod.desc=Nuclear core control rod\nHolds long rods of Silver, Boron, Cadmium, Indium, or Hafnium\nControlled by external redstone (0..15) or ProjectRed bundled cable (0..255)\nRight-click with screwdriver to cycle bundled input channel\n0 signal = 0%% insertion (retracted), max signal = 100%% insertion (full absorption)

# Item Tooltips
item.modularnuclear.radiovoltaic.plate.hv.desc=Converts absorbed neutron flux into direct HV electricity\nMax output: 1,024 EU/t (2A HV) via dynamo hatches
item.modularnuclear.radiovoltaic.plate.ev.desc=Converts absorbed neutron flux into direct EV electricity\nMax output: 4,096 EU/t (2A EV) via dynamo hatches
item.modularnuclear.radiovoltaic.plate.common.desc=Absorbs 100%% of incident neutron flux\nFast neutrons yield 4x electricity vs thermal neutrons\nExcess absorbed energy converts directly into core heat
item.modularnuclear.sensorcard.target=Target: [%d, %d, %d]
item.modularnuclear.sensorcard.unlinked=Unlinked. Right-click on MPTR reactor to bind.
item.modularnuclear.sensorkit.desc=Right-click on MPTR reactor to link and create sensor card

